an6.43:6.1 starts: He, having gone beyond all dhammas,
an6.43:6.2 starts: to whom human beings pay homage,
an6.43:6.3 starts: the devas pay homage as well—
an6.43:6.4 starts: so I have heard from the Worthy One
an6.43:16.1 starts: Like a white lotus,
# superseded: an6.43:16.2 starts: born & growing in the water,
# superseded: an6.43:16.3 starts: but not smeared by the water
# superseded: an6.43:16.4 starts: —fragrant, delightful—
an6.43:19.1 starts: Conveying an instructive meaning,
an6.43:19.2 starts: this image is taught by the observant.
an6.43:19.3 starts: Great nāgas will recognize
an6.43:19.4 starts: the nāga as taught by the nāga
an6.45:19.1 starts: Then they hound him—
an6.45:19.2 starts: painful mental resolves
an6.45:19.3 starts: born of remorse—
an6.45:19.4 starts: at home or in the wilderness.
an6.45:24.1 starts: is, in the discipline of the noble ones,
an6.45:24.2 starts: said to be living in ease.
an6.45:24.3 starts: Gaining a pleasure not of the flesh,
an6.45:24.4 starts: he determines on equanimity,
an6.55:21.1 starts: As a single mass of rock isn’t moved
an6.55:21.2 starts: even so all
an6.55:21.3 starts: forms, flavors, sounds,
an6.55:21.4 starts: aromas, contacts,
an6.45:15.1 starts: Now, anyone with no conviction
an6.45:15.2 starts: in the discipline of the noble ones
an6.45:15.3 starts: no sense of shame,
an6.45:15.4 starts: contemplating evil actions,
an6.45:23.1 starts: Now, anyone with conviction
an6.45:23.2 starts: firmly established
an6.45:23.3 starts: with a sense of shame,
an6.45:23.4 starts: discerning
an6.45:27.1 starts: In him, Such, rightly released,
an6.45:27.2 starts: there is the knowledge,
an6.45:27.3 starts: in the total ending
an6.45:27.4 starts: ‘My release
an6.49:5.1 starts: “Not as higher, lower, nor equal
an6.49:5.2 starts: do they refer to themselves.
an6.49:5.3 starts: With birth ended,
an6.49:5.4 starts: they go about
an7.7:4.1 starts: Whoever, man or woman, has these treasures,
an7.7:4.2 starts: has great treasure in the world
an7.7:4.3 starts: that no being,
an7.7:4.4 starts: human or divine,
an7.7:5.1 starts: So conviction & virtue, faith & Dhamma-vision
an7.7:5.2 none
an7.7:5.3 starts: should be cultivated by the intelligent,
an7.7:5.4 starts: remembering the Buddhas’ instruction.
